{"title": "Tarquin", "pageid": 56015, "url": "https://bg3.wiki/wiki/Tarquin", "categories": ["Mentioned characters", "Divinity references"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><aside class=\"portable-infobox noexcerpt searchaux pi-background pi-theme-default pi-layout-default pi-type-creature\"><h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title\" data-source=\"name\">Tarquin</h2><figure class=\"pi-item pi-media pi-image\" data-source=\"image\">\n\t<a href=\"/w/images/0/09/Tarquin_Body.png\" class=\"image image-thumbnail\" title=\"Tarquin Body.png\">\n\t\t<img src=\"/w/images/thumb/0/09/Tarquin_Body.png/300px-Tarquin_Body.png.webp\" srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/0/09/Tarquin_Body.png/300px-Tarquin_Body.png.webp 1x, /w/images/thumb/0/09/Tarquin_Body.png/600px-Tarquin_Body.png.webp 2x\" class=\"pi-image-thumbnail\" alt=\"Tarquin Body.png\" width=\"259\" height=\"500\">\n\t\t\n\t</a>\n\t\n</figure><div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"identity\">\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Identity</h3>\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Male</div>\n</div><div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"faction\">\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Faction</h3>\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Black Ring</div>\n</div><div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"hometown\">\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Hometown</h3>\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://dos2.wiki/wiki/Rivellon\">Rivellon</a></div>\n</div><div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"occupation\">\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Occupation</h3>\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Necromancer</div>\n</div><section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\"><h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Stats</h2><div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"race\">\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Race</h3>\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Human\" title=\"Human\">Human</a></div>\n</div></section></aside>\n\n<b>Tarquin</b> is a necromancer from Divinity: Original Sin 2 who, through unknown means, made his way to <a href=\"/wiki/Faer%C3%BBn\" title=\"Faerûn\">Faerûn</a>. While he does not appear in Baldur's Gate 3 directly, he did interact with characters and places the party can encounter.\n\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r356266\">.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote{display:grid;margin:10px 4px}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-left,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-right{padding:8px 16px;margin:auto}@media screen and (max-width:779px){.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-left,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-right{margin-top:10px;padding:8px 2px;border-left:0!important;grid-row:2;grid-column:2}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-image-right,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-image-left{margin:auto;grid-row:1;grid-column:2}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-author{grid-row:3;grid-column:2}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote{justify-content:center!important}}@media screen and (min-width:780px){.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-left{margin-left:10px;border-left:2px solid #3d3d3d!important;grid-row:1;grid-column:2}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-right{margin-right:10px;border-left:0!important;border-right:2px solid #3d3d3d;grid-row:1;grid-column:2}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-image-right{margin:auto 0;grid-row:1;grid-column:3}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-image-left{margin:auto 0;grid-row:1;grid-column:1}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-author{grid-row:2;grid-column:2}}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-author{margin-left:auto;margin-right:32px;font-size:smaller;font-weight:bold}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-begin,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-end{font-size:300%;font-family:serif;color:#3d3d3d;line-height:1em}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-begin{margin-bottom:auto;margin-right:8px}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-end{margin-top:auto;margin-left:8px}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-text{font-style:italic}</style><div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote\" style=\"justify-content: center\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-image-left\" style=\"display: inline-block; height: calc(70px + 2*4px); width: calc(70px + 2*4px); clip-path: polygon(50% 0%, 100% 50%, 50% 100%, 0% 50%); background: black;\"><span style=\"display: inline-block; margin: 4px; width: 70px; height: 70px; clip-path: polygon(50% 0%, 100% 50%, 50% 100%, 0% 50%);\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/14/Tarquin_Head.png/70px-Tarquin_Head.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/14/Tarquin_Head.png/105px-Tarquin_Head.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/14/Tarquin_Head.png/140px-Tarquin_Head.png.webp 2x\"><img src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/14/Tarquin_Head.png/70px-Tarquin_Head.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/1/14/Tarquin_Head.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span><blockquote style=\"font-size: 100%\" class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-left\">\n  <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center\">\n     <div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-begin\">“</div>\n     <div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-text\">The Gods merely feed upon our achievements like carrion birds.</div>\n     <div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-end\">„</div>\n  </div>\n</blockquote><div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-author\">— <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Tarquin</a></div><div style=\"grid-column:3\"></div></div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Involvement\">Involvement</span></h2>\n<h3><span id=\"Baldur.27s_Gate_3\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Baldur's_Gate_3\">Baldur's Gate 3</span></h3>\nCorrespondence between <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Lenore_De_Hurst\" title=\"Lenore De Hurst\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/6a/Sussur_Bloom_Faded.png/25px-Sussur_Bloom_Faded.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/6a/Sussur_Bloom_Faded.png/38px-Sussur_Bloom_Faded.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/6a/Sussur_Bloom_Faded.png/50px-Sussur_Bloom_Faded.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Lenore De Hurst\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/6a/Sussur_Bloom_Faded.png/25px-Sussur_Bloom_Faded.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/6a/Sussur_Bloom_Faded.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Lenore_De_Hurst\" title=\"Lenore De Hurst\">Lenore De Hurst</a> and <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Lorroakan\" title=\"Lorroakan\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/3/3e/Portrait_Lorroakan.png/25px-Portrait_Lorroakan.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/3/3e/Portrait_Lorroakan.png/38px-Portrait_Lorroakan.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/3/3e/Portrait_Lorroakan.png/50px-Portrait_Lorroakan.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Lorroakan\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/3/3e/Portrait_Lorroakan.png/25px-Portrait_Lorroakan.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/3/3e/Portrait_Lorroakan.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Lorroakan\" title=\"Lorroakan\">Lorroakan</a> describes an encounter with Tarquin which may have been his arrival on Toril:<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r356266\"><div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote\" style=\"justify-content: center\"><blockquote style=\"font-size: 110%\" class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-left\">\n  <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center\">\n     <div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-begin\">“</div>\n     <div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-text\">I swear it to be true, Lorroakan. I was on the very cusp of joining my fellow Mystrans for the ritual, when, CRASH! Right on top of me fell a gangle of tousled hair and magic most strange. Just then, something happened I can hardly describe, so foreign was the Weave - no, not Weave at all! - that ensnared me. This fellow - I didn't quite catch his name (something with a T and Q... Tuqueen?) - created some manner of anomaly that temporarily trapped me twixt our world and who-knows-where. Tell me, have you ever heard of such a thing?</div>\n     <div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-end\">„</div>\n  </div>\n</blockquote><div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-author\">— <a href=\"/wiki/A_Query_from_DeHurst\" title=\"A Query from DeHurst\">A Query from DeHurst</a></div><div style=\"grid-column:3\"></div></div>\nHe visited the <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/House_of_Grief\" title=\"House of Grief\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/0/02/Custom_Map_Icon.png/25px-Custom_Map_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/0/02/Custom_Map_Icon.png/38px-Custom_Map_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/0/02/Custom_Map_Icon.png/50px-Custom_Map_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"House of Grief\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/0/02/Custom_Map_Icon.png/25px-Custom_Map_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/0/02/Custom_Map_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span>⁠<a href=\"/wiki/House_of_Grief\" title=\"House of Grief\">House of Grief</a> under the pseudonym <i>Marco Creenn</i><sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>, and undertook the <a href=\"/wiki/Mapping_of_the_Heart\" title=\"Mapping of the Heart\">Mapping of the Heart</a>, resulting in the following entry in the Client List: <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r356266\"><div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote\" style=\"justify-content: center\"><blockquote style=\"font-size: 110%\" class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-left\">\n  <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center\">\n     <div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-begin\">“</div>\n     <div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-text\">Marco Creenn (possible false name) - curious sort, not local, by accent. Black hair, pale complexion - prying heart. Paid in full with unknown gold currency and was referred for Unburdening, but fled. \n<p>Note: <a href=\"/wiki/Viconia_DeVir\" title=\"Viconia DeVir\">Mother V</a> has ordered we seek out this 'Marco Creenn' if possible; during his Mapping, she detected thoughts and memories of strange lands and unfamiliar people. Fixated on a sword<sup id=\"cite_ref-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> - or possibly <i>zord(?)</i> Mother V's interest was piqued - she wants that mind. \n</p>\nUpdate: The trail has gone cold. It is as if he vanished entirely.</div>\n     <div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-end\">„</div>\n  </div>\n</blockquote><div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-author\">— <a href=\"/wiki/Client_List\" title=\"Client List\">Client List</a></div><div style=\"grid-column:3\"></div></div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Divinity:_Original_Sin_2\">Divinity: Original Sin 2</span></h3>\n<p>Somewhat uniquely, Tarquin is a double Easter Egg. In <i>Divinity: Original Sin 2's</i> post-game, his dialogue foreshadows Baldur's Gate 3, which was then in development, and lends credence to the idea that the above references are not only allusions to Tarquin, but that he also succeeded in traveling to Faerûn:\n</p>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r356266\"><div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote\" style=\"justify-content: center\"><blockquote style=\"font-size: 110%\" class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-left\">\n  <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center\">\n     <div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-begin\">“</div>\n     <div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-text\">How does one top the greatest feat of necromancy ever conceived? I might have the answer to that... tell me, have you ever heard of Gustavchen?<sup id=\"cite_ref-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> No, of course you wouldn't. It's a written language, unreadable to most... but myself, naturally. It comes from a mysterious race from another world - <a href=\"/wiki/Mind_flayers\" title=\"Mind flayers\">beings</a> that <b>feed</b> on minds. I intend to seek them out. This Gustavchen seems to guard portals to their realm. And once I've uncovered one, well... why settle for being the greatest mind in just one world, when there's another for the taking?</div>\n     <div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-end\">„</div>\n  </div>\n</blockquote><div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-author\">— Tarquin</div><div style=\"grid-column:3\"></div></div>\n<div style=\"clear: both;\"></div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notes\">Notes</span></h2>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r345964\">.mw-parser-output .reflist .references{list-style-type:inherit}.mw-parser-output .refs-act1::before{content:\"Act 1\";text-decoration:none;background:none;font-size:100%;font-weight:bold;direction:ltr}.mw-parser-output .refs-act2::before{content:\"Act 2\";text-decoration:none;background:none;font-size:100%;font-weight:bold;direction:ltr}.mw-parser-output .refs-act3::before{content:\"Act 3\";text-decoration:none;background:none;font-style:italic;font-size:100%;font-weight:bold;direction:ltr}.mw-parser-output .refs-url::before{content:\"External links\";text-decoration:none;background:none;font-size:100%;font-weight:bold;direction:ltr}.mw-parser-output .refs-text::before{content:\"Literature\";text-decoration:none;background:none;font-size:100%;font-weight:bold;direction:ltr}.mw-parser-output .refs-note::before{content:\"Notes\";text-decoration:none;background:none;font-size:100%;font-weight:bold;direction:ltr}</style><div class=\"reflist refs-nogroup\" style=\"list-style-type:decimal;\"><div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"> An anagram for \"Necromancer\" </span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-2\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"> Tarquin's fixation during the events of Divinity: Original Sin 2 is the sword <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://dos2.wiki/wiki/Anathema\">Anathema</a> </span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-3\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"> Gustavchen being a reference to \"Project Gustav\", the internal project name of Baldur's Gate 3 at Larian Studios; Gustav itself is named after CEO Swen Vincke's dog, who is also the source of the default custom character name 'Tav' </span>\n</li>\n</ol></div></div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"External_Links\">External Links</span></h2>\n<ul><li><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://dos2.wiki/wiki/Tarquin\">Tarquin</a> - Divinity: Original Sin 2 Wiki</li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Marco_Creenn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/22px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/33px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/44px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Marco Creenn\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/22px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-extlink\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Marco_Creenn\">Marco Creenn</a></span> on the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Main_Page\">Forgotten Realms Wiki</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260715000336\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [vary‐revision‐sha1, no‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.124 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.127 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 4319/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 43946/4194304 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 17739/4194304 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 18/200\nExpensive parser function count: 3/750\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11976/5000000 bytes\nExtLoops count: 0/1000\nLua time usage: 0.018/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 1074803/52428800 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%  116.073      1 -total\n 66.14%   76.770      1 Template:Infobox_creature\n 39.84%   46.238      1 Template:Infobox_creature/internal\n 23.16%   26.881      2 Template:Hidden